/// Static behavioral API documentation for the Honey Do's backend.
///
/// This mixin exposes a single read-only `getApiDoc` query. The document is a
/// static Markdown literal authored from the current backend source; it reads
/// no actor state and never changes at runtime.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend's behavioral API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Honey Do's Backend API\n\nHoney Do's is a handyman job-request service. Guests submit job requests\nwithout an account and track them with a public reference code. An\nadministrator signs in to quote, schedule, and progress those jobs, manage the\nbee crew, assign bees to jobs, enroll customers in the monthly package, and\nreview each customer's visit history.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- **Guest endpoints** (`submitRequest`, `getRequestByReference`, `acceptQuote`,\n  `createDepositCheckoutSession`, `confirmDepositPayment`, `recordDeposit`,\n  `confirmAppointment`, `submitReview`, `getVisitHistory`) require no sign-in.\n  They are callable by anonymous and signed-in callers alike.\n- **Admin endpoints** (`listRequests`, `getRequest`, `setQuote`,\n  `scheduleAppointment`, `advanceStatus`, `getDashboardStats`, `createBee`,\n  `updateBee`, `listBees`, `assignBeeToJob`, `setPackageEnrollment`,\n  `getCustomerVisitHistory`) require a signed-in caller whose principal holds\n  the `#admin` role. An anonymous caller or a signed-in caller without the role\n  is rejected with the trap\n  `Unauthorized: Only admins can perform this action`.\n- **OQL endpoints** (`schema`, `execute`) are provided by the OQL `Expose`\n  mixin. Two entities are registered: `jobRequest` (the job-request table) and\n  `bee` (the bee/employee table). Both are registered `controllerOnly`, so only\n  the platform controller (the Data Intelligence agent) can read them; end\n  users cannot query them directly.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nThe app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds\nthe user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app\nprincipal against that origin, for example:\n\n```\nicp identity link web <name> --app <host>\n```\n\nSuch a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it\nexpires.\n\nRegistration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own\nfrontend. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to\nthe app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a\ndifferent principal than the one the frontend registered. A direct API caller\nmust therefore register before any role-guarded call: call\n`_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller. The first caller to do\nso receives the `#admin` role; later callers receive the default role. An\nunregistered or anonymous caller hitting a guarded endpoint receives the trap\n`Unauthorized: Only admins can perform this action`.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Timestamp` is an `Int` of nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`).\n- Monetary amounts (`Quote.amount`, `Deposit.amount`, `PackagePlan.monthlyPrice`)\n  are integer **cents** in USD. `19900` means $199.00.\n- `ReferenceCode` is a `Text` such as `HD-123456789`; it is the guest's public\n  tracking key and is not secret.\n- `PhotoId` is a `Text` object-storage key; `photoIds` is an array of them.\n- Optional fields use `?T` and are `null` when absent.\n- `ServiceCategory` is a variant: `#house`, `#yardPlants`, `#fixIt`,\n  `#cleanOrganize`, `#moveLift`, `#errands`, `#mowing`, `#showMe`.\n- `JobStatus` is a variant: `#requested`, `#quoted`, `#scheduled`,\n  `#inProgress`, `#completed`.\n- `PaymentMethod` is a variant: `#stripe`, `#cashApp`.\n- `JobRequestInput.ownParts` is a `Bool` set by the customer on `submitRequest`\n  when they supply their own parts/supplies. It is immutable and visible to the\n  owner on the job view.\n- `Quote.discountApplied` is a `Bool` and `Quote.discountAmount` is a `Nat` in\n  cents. When `ownParts` is true, `setQuote` applies a 10% discount:\n  `discountAmount = amount / 10`, `Quote.amount` is the discounted total\n  (`amount - discountAmount`), and `discountApplied` is true. Otherwise\n  `discountApplied` is false and `discountAmount` is 0.\n\n## Job lifecycle and polling\n\nA job moves `#requested` -> `#quoted` -> `#scheduled` -> `#inProgress` ->\n`#completed`. `advanceStatus` (admin) moves one step forward and is a no-op at\n`#completed`. `setQuote` sets `#quoted`; `scheduleAppointment` sets `#scheduled`.\nWhen a job reaches `#completed`, `completedAt` is stamped and the visit is\nrecorded in the customer's visit history.\n\nGuests poll `getRequestByReference(referenceCode)` to observe progress. It is a\nquery and reads the latest committed state; a mutation issued immediately\nbefore it may not be visible to a query served by a different replica.\n\n## Visit history\n\n- `getVisitHistory(referenceCode)` returns the customer's completed visits for\n  that reference code, newest first. Each `VisitRecord` carries the job id, the\n  reference code, the service category, the assigned bee id and name (both\n  `null` when no bee was assigned), and the completion timestamp.\n- `getCustomerVisitHistory(id)` (admin) returns the same newest-first history\n  for the customer identified by the job's email address.\n- A visit is recorded automatically when a job reaches `#completed`; there is no\n  separate call to create one.\n\n## Bees (employees)\n\n- `createBee(input)` (admin) creates a bee with a `name` and `specialty` and\n  returns its `BeeView` with a generated `id`.\n- `updateBee(id, input)` (admin) replaces a bee's name and specialty.\n- `listBees()` (admin) returns all bees.\n- `assignBeeToJob(id, beeId)` (admin) assigns a bee to a job. The assigned bee's\n  name is surfaced to the customer as `assignedBeeName` on the job view.\n- Bee operations return `#notFound` when the bee or job does not exist.\n\n## Monthly package\n\nThe monthly package is a fixed monthly price covering a set number of visits\nper month. `setPackageEnrollment(id, active)` (admin) enrolls (`active = true`)\nor cancels (`active = false`) the customer on a job. Enrollment is surfaced to\nthe customer as `packageEnrollment` on the job view, including `active`,\n`monthlyPrice`, `includedVisits`, and `startedAt`. A guest can express interest\nin the package by setting `packageInterest = true` on `submitRequest`.\n\n## Request routing and contact\n\nEvery `submitRequest` emails the request details to the owner's inbox\n(`tanae022@gmail.com`) as soon as it is submitted. `setQuote` emails the\ncustomer. `scheduleAppointment` emails **both** the customer (at the address on\ntheir request) and the owner (`tanae022@gmail.com`). Email is the only\nnotification channel. Email delivery is best-effort: its result is ignored and\nnever blocks or fails the state change.\n\n## Deposits\n\nThe deposit is 50% of the accepted quote total (`Quote.amount`, already\ndiscounted). The active deposit path is CashApp: the customer sends the deposit\nto `$Taetae22Wright` and calls `recordDeposit(referenceCode, #cashApp)` to mark\nit sent; there is no confirmation-code field. The Stripe methods\n(`createDepositCheckoutSession`, `confirmDepositPayment`) remain available but\nare not surfaced in the app until Stripe is configured later.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `submitRequest` is **not** idempotent: each call creates a new job with a new\n  reference code. Retrying after a timeout creates a duplicate request.\n- `acceptQuote`, `recordDeposit`, `confirmAppointment`, `submitReview`,\n  `setQuote`, `scheduleAppointment`, and `advanceStatus` are safe to retry in\n  the sense that they converge on the same state, but `advanceStatus` is\n  **not** idempotent: each call advances one step, so a duplicate call moves the\n  job further along the lifecycle.\n- `confirmDepositPayment` is safe to call repeatedly: once the deposit is paid\n  it returns the current view without contacting Stripe again.\n- `createBee` is **not** idempotent: each call creates a new bee with a new id.\n- `updateBee`, `assignBeeToJob`, and `setPackageEnrollment` are safe to retry:\n  they overwrite the target state with the supplied values.\n\n## Errors, traps, and limits\n\n- `createDepositCheckoutSession` returns `#invalidState` when the quote has not\n  been accepted or the deposit is already paid, and `#paymentError` when Stripe\n  does not return a checkout session. It returns the raw Stripe JSON response\n  as `Text`; parse `id` and `url` from it and redirect with\n  `window.location.href`.\n- `confirmDepositPayment` returns `#paymentError` when Stripe reports the\n  session failed, and `#invalidState` when no deposit was started.\n- `isStripeConfigured` reports whether an admin has stored a Stripe secret key.\n  Deposit checkout traps with `Stripe needs to be first configured` until then.\n- `confirmAppointment` returns `#invalidState` when no appointment is scheduled.\n- `submitReview` returns `#invalidState` when the rating is outside 1-5 or the\n  job is not `#completed`.\n- Admin endpoints **trap** rather than returning an error variant when the\n  caller is not an admin.\n- `getApiDoc` is a static query; it never reflects runtime state.\n\n## OQL entities\n\nBoth entities are `controllerOnly` and are read through the OQL `schema()` and\n`execute()` query methods.\n\n- `jobRequest` (primary key `id`) exposes `assignedBeeId` (0 when unassigned),\n  `assignedBeeName` (empty when unassigned), `packageEnrollment` (`active`,\n  `cancelled`, or `none`), `packageActive` (Bool), `completedAt` (0 when not\n  completed), plus `referenceCode`, `customerName`, `email`, `phone`,\n  `category`, `description`, `preferredTiming`, `photoCount`, `createdAt`,\n  `ownParts` (Bool), `status`, `quoteAmount`, `quoteDiscountApplied` (Bool),\n  `quoteDiscountAmount` (cents), `depositPaid`, `appointmentAt`, and\n  `reviewRating`.\n- `bee` (primary key `id`) exposes `id`, `name`, `specialty`, and `createdAt`.\n"
  };
};
